gl32 G1, the x86 twin's runs (route i to vb 37,800), each summarised by vcsum32.py and compared with a reference run by the md5 of
its hash / picture / xlive / natb / natq / natz lines.  Notes:
 - a3 = MGS2_NAT_CYCLE=3,3,3,3, no cache;  b3 = a3 + MGS2_NAT_VC=3 with a 4,096 KB block and check mode.  b3 was run with the FIRST
   form of the static-stream check (a group's streams hashed again only when the group was next drawn, so after long waits: its
   'natst: CHANGED' lines, soonest 15 vblanks after the draw, at stage changes).  dc and g31 use the final form (every vblank's start
   for 8 vblanks after the draw): CHANGED 0.
 - da = a3 with the delivered MGS2_GL_DZ (so its picture lines differ from a3's, as expected);  dx = the delivered keys (the
   hashref's run);  dc = dx + check mode + the static check.
 - g31 = gl31's keys (MGS2_NAT_CYCLE=0,0,3,3, gl30's DZ) + MGS2_NAT_VC=3, check mode, static check, against gl31's own twin run b.
 - lw2 = a3 + MGS2_NAT_VC=3 + check mode in the PSP's late-walk mode (MGS2_NAT_LW=2: plan, copy, view); its per-turn 'natvc' lines
   are not printed in that mode, the totals line is: 'check: 1626878 compared, 0 DIFFER' (see below).  lw2b = the same with
   MGS2_NAT_VC=2 (streams in place, no cache).

